    </div>

    @*
        The "Application Database" section was removed here (2026-07-25).

        It presented the system's own database as a per-tenant setting, but nothing ever read
        those fields: every DbContext and Hangfire storage is built from
        ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection in appsettings.json at startup. The fields were only
        ever populated by parsing that same connection string for display.

        Editing them therefore appeared to repoint the application database and did nothing at
        all — the most expensive kind of control to leave in a settings screen. The system
        database is a deployment concern, not tenant configuration.
    *@

    <!-- Sync Schedule Settings -->
